{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION, recorded: keep 7b22 as a CHILD (so this ticket cannot close until the registry rework lands) and remediate this ticket's ACs to account for the rework. Both done. The AC block is now split into what this change delivered (9 items, including the guard-order fix the OSS survey identified as the real fix for the bug class) and what is DELEGATED to child 7b22 (3 items: registry membership, the unknown-provider diagnostic, and the enumerated back-compat). Note this makes epic 061c wait on 7b22 as well, since this ticket is an epic child — that coupling is intentional under this decision: the ticket's own criterion asked for the registered provider set and the shipped change does not provide it, so the ticket state should say so rather than closing on unmet criteria. Editing the description voided the plan-review attestation (stale-material); the claim gate was already satisfied and the completion verifier reads the current ACs, so no re-review is needed to continue — but a fresh review-plan would be needed if this ticket were ever re-claimed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785630103292397001,"uuid":"14169415-5e3f-4c89-b7df-a294b74bab7f"}